Building northstar for Debian
-----------------------------

The upstream build uses two meson wrap subprojects that `meson setup`
normally downloads at configure time: lexbor (HTML/URL engine) and
quickjs-ng (JavaScript engine). Debian builds run without network
access, and debhelper's meson buildsystem passes
--wrap-mode=nodownload, so the orig tarball must already contain the
subproject sources.

Meson applies the patches listed in each wrap's diff_files (from
subprojects/packagefiles/) when it downloads the subproject, and never
again, so the tarball has to carry the patched checkouts as they are on
disk. Neither `git archive` nor `meson dist` keeps those uncommitted
changes. Meson also never moves an existing checkout when a wrap's
revision changes, so check that every checkout matches its pin first.

The orig tarball is therefore a repack, versioned <version>+ds. It
also leaves out the render-test fixtures copied from Wikipedia, listed
under Files-Excluded in debian/copyright; nothing in the build uses
them. To produce it from a checkout of the upstream release tag:

    meson subprojects download lexbor quickjs-ng
    scripts/check-subprojects.sh
    tar --exclude-vcs --exclude='subprojects/*/.git' \
        --exclude='builddir*' --exclude='subprojects/quickjs' \
        --exclude='data/render-tests/assets/wiki-*' \
        --exclude='data/render-tests/assets/wikipedia-*.css' \
        --exclude='data/render-tests/realworld-wikipedia*.html' \
        --transform='s,^\.,northstar-<version>+ds,' \
        -cJf ../northstar_<version>+ds.orig.tar.xz .

If check-subprojects.sh reports a stale checkout, delete
subprojects/<name> and download it again.

The wuffs and plmpeg subprojects are vendored directly in the tree and
need no download. After that, `dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc` builds the
package the normal debhelper way.

debian/rules builds without H.264: only Cisco's prebuilt OpenH264
binaries carry Cisco's H.264 patent licence, and a distribution build
from source is not covered by it. AV1 (libdav1d) and VP9 (libvpx) are
enabled. The build date shown in the About dialog comes from
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, so the build is reproducible.
